      "side": 1,
      "message": "In `util/focaltech/updater.cc`, you correctly use an anonymous namespace `namespace { ... }` at the top of the file for helper functions like `ReadFileToVector` and `CalculateSha256`.\n\nHowever, right below that, you fall back to C-style `static` linkage for other helpers:\n\n```cpp\nstatic std::expected\u003cvoid, FtError\u003e FtErasePage(...)\nstatic std::expected\u003cvoid, FtError\u003e FtDownloadPage(...)\nstatic std::expected\u003cvoid, FtError\u003e FtDownloadBin(...)\n\n```\n\n**The Google C++ Style Guide explicitly states:** *\"Use internal linkage (anonymous namespaces) in .cc files. Do not use `static` for internal linkage of functions or variables.\"*\n\n**Recommendation:** Move `FtErasePage`, `FtDownloadPage`, `FtDownloadBin`, `FtMcuReset`, and `FtGetBootVersion` into the anonymous namespace at the top of the file and drop the `static` keyword.",
