      "writtenOn": "2026-06-04T00:29:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In `util/focaltech/updater.h`, you define a packed struct for firmware config:\n\n```cpp\nstruct FtConfigPage {\n  uint32_t code_valid_control_word;\n  uint8_t reserved[28];\n  uint32_t code_start_address;\n} __attribute__((packed));\n\n```\n\nWhile `__attribute__((packed))` prevents the compiler from adding padding, Google Style encourages pairing packed structs defining wire/hardware protocols with a `static_assert` to act as an un-ignorable unit test for struct layout. If someone accidentally changes `uint32_t` to `size_t` in the future, the build will immediately fail rather than flashing a corrupted config page.\n\n**Recommendation:**\nAdd this immediately below the struct definition:\n\n```cpp\nstatic_assert(sizeof(FtConfigPage) \u003d\u003d 36, \"FtConfigPage must be exactly 36 bytes\");\n\n```",
